From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:12:20 -0700
Subject: GPU: Reset base level before TexStorage in validating decoder

PowerVR GPUs have a driver bug when glTexStorage2D or glTexStorage3D
is called on a texture with a non-zero base level already applied.
This workaround resets the base level to zero before making the
TexStorage call, and restores the base level afterwards.

Bug: 551573368
Change-Id: I25eae6a9ed52fd123d3e65143bf99d4e3ea51322
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8298400
Auto-Submit: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1686868}

